				43,
				3
			],
			"Message": "style(Worker): Revert ESBuild configurations to readable PascalCase format\n\nThe ESBuild configuration files in `Configuration/ESBuild/` were inadvertently minified, compressing variable names to single letters (e.g., `i`, `o`, `t`, `e`, `r`, `n`) and collapsing control flow into dense blocks. This contradicts the project's strict PascalCase naming convention for all variables and functions, even in build scripts, and severely hampers readability and maintainability.\n\nRevert `Target.js` and `Configuration/ESBuild/Worker.js` to the expanded, readable format used in the source `Source/Configuration/ESBuild/Worker.js`. Ensure all local variables and exports follow PascalCase (e.g., `On`, `Clean`, `Default`). Restore descriptive destructuring and explicit control flow statements. The source configuration remains the source of truth, ensuring consistency across the Worker element's build pipeline without altering the underlying build logic or output behavior.",
			"SHA": "4504d626295c31070f8d2317b6a9801b356fb330"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T13:36:06Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				43,
				3
			],
			"Message": "style(Worker): Align ESBuild configurations with formatting standards\n\nReformat the ESBuild configuration files in the Worker element to match the project's strict formatting guidelines. This involves expanding compressed syntax into readable, multi-line structures in `Target.js` and `Source/Configuration/ESBuild/Worker.js`, renaming local variables to follow PascalCase conventions (e.g., `i` to `On`, `t` to `Current`), and removing redundant file duplication.\n\nThe changes also include deleting a redundant `Configuration/ESBuild/Worker.js` entry that conflicts with the source configuration and ensuring consistent export structures for the build pipeline. These adjustments improve code maintainability and readability within the build tooling layer without altering the underlying build logic or output behavior.",
			"SHA": "9031ee92a4f8d6ff5f09d3eaa26ba083c378cd5f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T06:20:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				43,
				7
			],
			"Message": "feat(Worker): Integrate development telemetry bridge and format configs\n\nIntroduce a dual-pipe telemetry system in the Worker element to capture service-worker lifecycle events (install, activate) and custom spans via PostHog and OTLP. The new Bridge.ts module uses lazy-loading to ensure zero production bundle impact while providing detailed debugging metrics in development.\n\nAlign the ESBuild configuration files (Target.js, Worker.js) with the project's formatting standards, expanding compressed syntax into a readable, multi-line structure without altering build logic. Update the CHANGELOG to reflect the current version history and architectural decisions for the workbench lift cycle.\n\nThis establishes the foundation for observability in the background processing layer while maintaining strict separation between debug instrumentation and runtime performance.",
			"SHA": "980fba85d52768e95dde75b29db16e206b0bf14f"
		},
